 "title": "Derivatives of Trigonometric Functions",
 "short": "Derivatives of Trigonometric Functions",
 "lead": "The <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivatives</span> of the sine and cosine come from the definition and two <span data-concept=\"important-trigonometric-limits\">trigonometric limits</span>; the <span data-concept=\"quotient-rule\">quotient rule</span> then gives the derivatives of the other four <span data-concept=\"trigonometric-functions\">trigonometric functions</span>, and the <span data-concept=\"higher-order-derivative\">higher-order derivatives</span> of sine and cosine are found to repeat.",
 "objectives": [
  "Find the derivatives of the sine and cosine function.",
  "Find the derivatives of the standard trigonometric functions.",
  "Calculate the higher-order derivatives of the sine and cosine."
 ],
 "summary_html": "<ul><li>We can find the <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivatives</span> of sin <em>x</em> and cos <em>x</em> by using the definition of <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivative</span> and the <span data-concept=\"limit\">limit</span> formulas found earlier. The results are $$\\frac{d}{dx}\\;\\sin x=\\cos x\\;\\frac{d}{dx}\\;\\cos x=-\\sin x.$$</li><li>With these two formulas, we can determine the <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivatives</span> of all six basic <span data-concept=\"trigonometric-functions\">trigonometric functions</span>.</li></ul>",
